{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793440000000-engineer-retained-ffi.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-16 14:30:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-16 21:30:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: G2: backends refuse a task with a retained FFI request before attach (uncommitted)\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-16 21:30 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: owner approved starting the gap-list follow-ups; codex implements, Fable reviews\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-retained-ffi (branch srvm-retained-ffi @ origin/master 6b001f87). Read ./collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md section 1.3 and row G2, docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md section 4.3 and 4.6 (limit 5, rows 4/7-9/17 are excluded by the harness only), UCF section 7.11 (\"refuse the unsupported remainder before attach\"). THE HAZARD: `layout/lower-defect` (src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc) refuses `:ambiguous-image`, `:installs`, `:free-env-value` and `:continuation-registers` but NOT a task carrying a retained FFI request; a backend receiver (debruijn/register.cljc, debruijn/stack.cljc) attaches it and it never wakes (the backends' `:request-sent` re-park builds the response wait over their own call pair, register.cljc ~:511, stack.cljc ~:567; the harness keeps row 4 out via `unlowerable #{[4 :stack] [4 :register]}` safepoint_harness_test ~:1711). DO: add a pre-attach refusal `{:yin.k/unsupported :retained-ffi}` (use the existing refusal vocabulary of lower-defect; name the slot as lower-defect names its siblings) so lowering such a task INTO a backend is refused with a named reason; do NOT widen the fragment and do NOT build the seam (owner ruling: not built). Determine from the code what \"retained FFI pending\" is in the task (the pending entry / wait kind of the :request-sent state; read how row 4 of the harness builds it and how semantic.cljc :105-109 honours a carried pair) and refuse exactly that, not other FFI states that legitimately lower. Tests: one refusal test per backend (stack and register) that builds the row-4 shaped task, asserts lower-defect / lower-task returns the named refusal, and a positive control that an FFI task WITHOUT a retained request still lowers; update the harness `unlowerable` table only if its meaning changes (prefer: keep the table, add the refusal assertion that the row-4 pair is now refused by the gate, not just excluded); update docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md section 4.6 limit-5 sentence and UCF 7.11 only to say the gate now exists (one sentence each, keep wording minimal). NOT allowed: src/yang, test/yang, widening backends, collab commits. No pinned hash/golden may move; if one does, STOP and report. No commit/stage. Foreground lanes: kondo on changed files (0 new); `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.semantic.layout-test -n yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.register-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-test -n yin.vm.semantic.effects-test`; whole JVM quick tier `clojure -M:test -e :slow` (loopback: request unrestricted). No Node/Dart (orchestrator). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-retained-ffi.report.md with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID, diff summary, counts, mutant proof (remove the refusal: the tests fail), truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
