{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short; rg -n '1.3|G2|7.11|limit|retained|4.3|4.6' collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; rg --files | rg 'UCF|ucf|universal.*continu|AGENTS.md|layout_test|safepoint_harness|layout.cljc'\"","aggregated_output":"?? collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md\n?? collab/1793440000000-engineer-retained-ffi.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1793440000000-engineer-retained-ffi.prompt.md\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:19:- **X2 (b)** the two de Bruijn backends silently hang, rather than refuse, a task carrying a retained FFI request (row 4): the exclusion is harness-only, not a pre-attach gate (§1.3). Half a day converts it to a named refusal without widening the fragment.\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:20:- **X3 (b, owner-gated)** three capability questions the owner has deferred: any-pc snapshots / `:running` roots under custody (slice 6d, §1.2), the REPL's own export into its custody composition (UCF §7.11 \"yin.repl.core handoff composition\", §1.1), and the backend fragment (retained-FFI seam, §1.3).\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:21:- **X4 (evidence)** no Dart slow-tier run is on record for phase 8; the 89/61/350 harness laws, the C4 execution oracle and the Stage E kill rows have JVM and Node evidence only (§4.2).\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:29:**What the gap was.** Until 8c the REPL's `:semantic` evaluator was the old stack-shaped v3 kernel and its two de Bruijn evaluators were fed through `packet->named-datoms` and the old lowerers (phase-8 plan §1.7, risk 5). The row carrier of phases 6-7 (`rows/lift-task`, `rows/lower-task`) lifts only the register kernel's frames, so nothing a REPL session ran could be exported into custody. The owner accepted that until phase 8 (orchestrator log :11250; continuation §8.4 :2200-2201; UCF §7.11 :3366).\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:35:- Every machine the REPL runs is therefore a `SemanticVM` (or a backend over an A-derived image) that `rows/lift-task` (`ucf/rows.cljc:1737`) and `layout/lift-task` accept. Continuation §8.4 :2183-2186 records the closure at 8c; that text matches the code.\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:37:**Qualification (b).** The REPL carries a custody composition only as data: `repl.cljc:880-886` (\"the shell only carries it ... Nothing in the shell reads or steps it\"), stepped by `repl/main.cljc:962-1004`. There is no REPL command that exports the session's evaluator machine into that composition (`command-heads`, `repl.cljc:239-240`: no `export`). So the gap is closed in the sense the owner ruled (the kernel the REPL runs is liftable) and UCF §7.11 :3381-3383 is still accurate: \"still owed ... the `yin.repl.core` handoff composition\". Effort if wanted: an `(export)` command plus `holder/export` wiring and one `dht_process_test` row, 2-3 days. Risk of leaving: none to the kernel; a product gap only.\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:44:- `ucf/holder/export.cljc:107-112, 128-135` `first-refusal`/`enter`: the holder refuses to enter exporting unless every machine of the tree is quiescent.\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:48:**Feasibility of slice 6d (b).** The kernel's between-instruction state is already a closed data shape: `vm-hot` with fuel returns `put-registers machine seg pc W E K` (`semantic.cljc:142-143, 50-55`), so a snapshot `{seg pc W E K}` exists at every instruction boundary and `analysis/live` (`analysis.cljc:86-89`) gives its window as `L(pc)` with no `rd` subtraction. What a slice must add:\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:53:| validator branch | `frame.cljc:133-140` (`:site`, `:destination`, `:deliver`, `window-defect`) | `window-self` does not apply; `window-extra/missing` against `L(pc)` |\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:56:| custody by kind | `rows.cljc:1701-1713` `header-custody`, `custody-baseline :1286`, holder `at-safepoint?` `driver.cljc:2147`, `export/enter` | a running root has no retained writes, so `protect!` is vacuous; the holder's `:safepoint` phase needs a `:running`-snapshot entry |\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:62:### 1.3 Fork custody slot and the retained-FFI seam\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:72:- Design: continuation §4.3 :917-948, §4.6 limit 5, §11 6c Q2.\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:73:- **Risk of leaving it, and the one real finding here.** Continuation §4.6 (:1097-1109) says plainly that rows 4, 7-9 and 17 \"are excluded by the harness only, not by a general pre-attach fragment gate\". `layout/lower-defect` refuses `:ambiguous-image`, `:installs`, `:free-env-value` and `:continuation-registers`, not a retained FFI pending. A real composition that lowers a row-4-shaped task into a backend receiver attaches it and it never wakes (codex probe 3 reproduced the hang on all four such pairs). UCF §7.11 :2923-2924 requires backends \"to refuse the unsupported remainder before attach\". The owner's \"refuse-the-remainder requirement is not evidence of a general gate\" (continuation :1109) records the discrepancy but leaves the hazard.\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:74:- What a future need would trigger: the four-line seam itself (half a day, raises law 5 to 366/96) if any composition migrates retained-FFI tasks into backends. Independent of that: a pre-attach refusal `:yin.k/unsupported :retained-ffi` in `lower-defect` (half a day, one refusal test per backend) is compliant with \"not widened\" and closes the silent-hang hazard. Recommended (§6 item 2).\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:80:| 1 Identity | `2daa17fb` exists; `linker.cljc:2123-2134` `relowered` recomputes H/R from the tree's projection, `:2203` verifies against it; the native format records use `image-hash`/`register-hash` only as `:identity-matches-fn` for an image against its own checksum (`linker.cljc:664-665, 682-684`), while the semantic record's identity is `jing/segment-key` (`:697`); final report rows 6/13 | **met** |\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:83:| 4 Evaluator | transitions of §2.4 as code: `semantic.cljc:149-268` (saved window on a non-tail call `:186-188`; tail call through `K` `:206-210`; abortive continuation `:213-218` with ownership via `engine/operator-kind` `engine.cljc:77-90`; `:ffi-call :234-254`; `:park :259-261`; `:resume` accepts a halted result `:265`); restore helper with both delivery modes `:101-126` and the deferred-tail halt environment from `base` `:123-124`; parity `parity_test.cljc:80-228` (B0 values, corpus outcomes, Rule R, continuations, FFI, streams), trace alignment `walker_trace_test.cljc:113-152`, `vm_test.cljc:116-209` (tail grows no frame, `rd` written once, tail primitive through `K`, define through the module store) | **met** |\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:85:| 6 Continuation format | `frame.cljc:80-181` implements every rule §4.2 lists (representation `:105-108`, body scope `:58`, membership `:59-61`, site `:135-137`, destination `:138`, delivery mode `:139/:143` with `tail` carrying no window or env `:89, :97`, return-frame sites `:148-151`, pending/reason `:162-173`, free-env `:155-161`); row shapes `rows.cljc:58-61` are §4.2's (`:act [A pc env window k rd]`, `:tail [A site k]`, keyed `:window`, `:kframe`), root `free-env` slot `:67`; harness 89 cases `safepoint_harness_test.cljc:656-669`, 61/350 on the native lanes `:1691-1703, :1778-1789` | **met at the accepted matrix** (a: 61/350) |\ncollab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:86:| 7 Stage D/E | `ucf/stage_e_rows_test.cljc:36-105`, `stage_e_process_test.clj:257-309` (JVM-only process matrix), `crash_cut_test`, `durability_test`, `fencing_rows_test`, `compose_rows_test`; jupiter four